/T (Another armistice was signed in 1949, and the Line of Control \(LoC\) was established, which was supposed to serve as the border between the two countries. However, the LoC was only intended as a temporary measure, and in 1972, the Simla Agreement was signed, which came into force after the 1971 War. According to this document, Jammu and Kashmir were formally divided between India and Pakistan. Nevertheless, neither side was willing to acknowledge it as a permanent boundary. )
