/P 161 0 R
/E (India and Pakistan became the fifth and sixth nuclear states in the world, and the international community has consistently condemned these tests. On June 6, 1998, the UN Security Council issued a unanimous resolution condemning these tests. The resolution demands that India and Pakistan abandon their nuclear ambitions, stop their nuclear tests, adhere to the Non-Proliferation Treaty and the Comprehensive Test Ban Treaty, and resume dialogue on all issues, including Kashmir. However, despite this resolution, the situation between India and Pakistan was destined to worsen. )
/Pg 16 0 R
