/P 161 0 R
/E (The conflict between India and Pakistan ended only after enormous diplomatic pressure from the international community, including the United States. Thus, Pakistan agreed to withdraw its troops from Indian-administered Kashmir, and after three weeks of fighting, Indian troops managed to capture Tiger Hill, which was strategically the most advantageous point for the Pakistani army. On July 14, 1999, declaredOperation Vijay successful and formally ended hostilities on July 26, 1999. The territorial dispute between India and Pakistan continues to be one of the most dangerous sources of tension in international relations. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
