438 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 169 0 R
/E (Thefirstmajor attemptto manage the Indo-Pakistani conflict was the Simla Agreement of 1972. India and Pakistan agreed to settle their differences peacefully and through bilateral negotiations after the 1971 war. The agreement also defined the Line of Control in Kashmir. The agreement helped to cool tensions after the war, but it failed to solve the dispute over Kashmir. Since the agreement left the dispute settlement fully to bilateral negotiations, there was no mechanism to take care of this dispute if negotiations failed. Future solutions should take note of the mechanisms that will ensure bilateral negotiations continue to take place and that the United Nations can help in times of crisis. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
