610 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (The primary objective of the Committee for Topic B is coordination of binding and global effort to dismantle transnational terrorist networks after the August 1998 bombings of U.S. Embassies in Nairobi and Dar es Salaam. The delegates need to address the threats of non-state actors by cutting off sources of their financing \(including informal networks such as hawala\), denying them safe havens and creating efficient intelligence-sharing mechanisms under the UNSC Resolutions 1214 and 1267. Notably, the proposed solutions should be balanced between harsh multilateral counter-terrorism measures and respect for national sovereignty in the light of Article 2\(4\) of the UN Charter and self-defense provisions of Article 51. Based on the analysis of previous diplomatic pressure, sources and sponsors of regimes, and unilateral actions, the delegates need to develop realistic UN-based mechanisms of pushing state compliance, accountability of hostile regimes and maintenance of global peace and security. )
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
